  const DATA_TYPE diag_row = one + two * a; /* used in row sweep    */

  /* Parallelize over 'i' (spatial dimension) for each time step.
     Each (i) line forms an independent tridiagonal solve in both
     sweeps, so there are no cross-i dependencies within a given
     time step.

     A single parallel region over all time steps reduces thread
     creation/destruction overhead. Implicit barriers at the end
     of each 'omp for' ensure that:
       - the row sweep starts only after the column sweep finishes
         for all i at a given t;
       - the next time step starts only after both sweeps complete. */
